    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0686" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.6363/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Howell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-23T15:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 23,
                                1927—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 23—12:40
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Your telegram No. 4, February 4th [<hi rendition="#italic">3rd</hi>].
                    Investigation discloses no direct action upon part of British and Belgian
                        colleagues.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d640-f1"/> Latter favorable to joint
                    action. British considering what steps if any should be taken. They seemed
                    impressed with the irregularities pointed out and indicated arguments to be used
                    in justice to companies complying with the law and danger to plants operated by
                    these companies. It is believed floating storage with little investment has
                    caused petroleum products to be sold at a lower figure than would otherwise
                    obtain. Recommend that no further action be taken until the British reply to my
                    memorandum left with the High Commissioner.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d640-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d640-f1" n="27" xml:id="d640-f1-content">
                <p>In his telegram No. 8, Feb. 25, 1927, 9 a.m. (file No. 883.6363/27), the Minister
                    stated: “Belgian colleague represents Roumanian interests”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d640-f2" n="28" xml:id="d640-f2-content">
                <p>Copy not found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
